{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788459744252,"sessionID":"ses_f977ec03affetTdEA9a1zaz0iY","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-a2f16a313ea57681","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"gh issue view 149","workdir":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-format-research"},"output":"title:\tImplement Float (IEEE binary64 per ADR 0007) across the backends\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tkantord (Dániel Kántor)\nlabels:\t\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t149\n--\nBuild the Float type end to end, per docs/adr/0007-float-is-javascripts-double.md: IEEE 754\nbinary64, matching JavaScript's number representation, no alternative width, no decimal type.\n\nSemantics per gh:145 (the Q37 ruling): admit NaN/Infinity, division by zero returns Infinity\n(IEEE), matching IEEE 754. Division is a total function on Float; Int and Float division have\ndifferent failure behavior (Int still raises on zero divisor).\n\nNot yet settled, needs a call during implementation: exact float literal printing so all seven\nbackends agree byte for byte (default float formatting differs across languages) -- pick a\nformat and hold every backend to it. See draft.md Q37 in plans/questions.md for the fuller\nquestion shape if it still exists, otherwise use the ADR and gh:145 as the source of truth.\n\nAcceptance:\n- Float literals parse and type-check\n- arithmetic (+ - * /) and comparisons work across all seven backends with agreeing output\n- NaN/Infinity are producible and print identically across backends\n- division by zero on Float returns Infinity, not an error (contrast with Int)\n- corpus test coverage added for the above\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","metadata":{"output":"title:\tImplement Float (IEEE binary64 per ADR 0007) across the backends\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tkantord (Dániel Kántor)\nlabels:\t\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t149\n--\nBuild the Float type end to end, per docs/adr/0007-float-is-javascripts-double.md: IEEE 754\nbinary64, matching JavaScript's number representation, no alternative width, no decimal type.\n\nSemantics per gh:145 (the Q37 ruling): admit NaN/Infinity, division by zero returns Infinity\n(IEEE), matching IEEE 754. Division is a total function on Float; Int and Float division have\ndifferent failure behavior (Int still raises on zero divisor).\n\nNot yet settled, needs a call during implementation: exact float literal printing so all seven\nbackends agree byte for byte (default float formatting differs across languages) -- pick a\nformat and hold every backend to it. See draft.md Q37 in plans/questions.md for the fuller\nquestion shape if it still exists, otherwise use the ADR and gh:145 as the source of truth.\n\nAcceptance:\n- Float literals parse and type-check\n- arithmetic (+ - * /) and comparisons work across all seven backends with agreeing output\n- NaN/Infinity are producible and print identically across backends\n- division by zero on Float returns Infinity, not an error (contrast with Int)\n- corpus test coverage added for the above\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"gh issue view 149","time":{"start":1788459744249,"end":1788459744251}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"So the issue is gh:149 — \"float-format-research\" maps to the float-build-* lanes. But wait, the brief says the issue is \"float-format-research\" but the board references gh:149 (the float-build lanes). Let me re-read the brief.\n\n\"Your task is GitHub issue #float-format-research: run `gh issue view float-format-research` and read every comment before touching anything.\"\n\nSo the issue ID is \"float-format-research\" — but `gh issue view` only accepts numbers. The issue is likely gh:149 based on the board. The `gh issue view float-format-research` failed because gh requires a number.\n\nLet me try `gh issue view 149` to get the actual issue. Also let me look at the existing JS reference float-build. The board mentions float-build as a dependency. Let me find it.\n\nActually wait — let me re-read the task: \"Survey how Go (strconv.FormatFloat/ParseFloat), Python (repr(float)/float(str)), and Rust (Display/Debug impls, str::parse) each format an IEEE binary64 float to a string and back versus the already-landed JS reference, focusing on round-trip precision and hex/exponent edge cases.\"\n\nSo the JS reference is already landed. I need to find it. Let me look at the source tree for the JS backend and the float implementation.\n\nLet me run `gh issue view 149` and explore the source structure.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_06881f7d10016qFu6bLC77JP1b","sessionID":"ses_f977ec03affetTdEA9a1zaz0iY","messageID":"msg_06881ddae001K664Iz3QDaY6Kf"}}
